    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.statusline\n\n### Description\n\nWhen we call `require(\"mini.statusline\").setup(opts)`, the plugin is loaded, but the status is not drawn. This causes issues when I try to lazy load using `lazy.nvim` which loads the plugin after `WinEnter`. To get it to draw the initial status, I have to add this after the setup as a hack.\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.cmd([[do WinEnter]])\r\n```\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.5\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n-- minimal.lua\r\n-- DO NOT change the paths and don't remove the colorscheme\r\nlocal root = vim.fn.fnamemodify(\"./.repro\", \":p\")\r\n\r\n-- set stdpaths to use .repro\r\nfor _, name in ipairs({ \"config\", \"data\", \"state\", \"cache\" }) do\r\n\tvim.env[(\"XDG_%s_HOME\"):format(name:upper())] = root .. \"/\" .. name\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- bootstrap lazy\r\nlocal lazypath = root .. \"/plugins/lazy.nvim\"\r\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(lazypath) then\r\n\tvim.fn.system({ \"git\", \"clone\", \"--filter=blob:none\", \"https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim.git\", lazypath })\r\nend\r\nvim.opt.runtimepath:prepend(lazypath)\r\n\r\nlocal config = require(\"config\")\r\nvim.opt.laststatus = 2\r\n\r\nrequire(\"lazy\").setup({\r\n\t{\r\n\t\t\"catppuccin/nvim\",\r\n\t\tname = \"catppuccin\",\r\n\t\tlazy = false,\r\n\t\tpriority = 1000,\r\n\t\topts = {\r\n\t\t\tintegrations = {\r\n\t\t\t\tmini = true,\r\n\t\t\t},\r\n\t\t},\r\n\t\tconfig = function(_, opts)\r\n\t\t\trequire(\"catppuccin\").setup(opts)\r\n\t\t\tvim.cmd.colorscheme(\"catppuccin\")\r\n\t\tend,\r\n\t},\r\n\t{\r\n\t\t\"echasnovski/mini.statusline\",\r\n\t\tevent = \"VeryLazy\",\r\n\t\topts = {\r\n\t\t\t-- Do not override vim settings.\r\n\t\t\tset_vim_settings = false,\r\n\t\t},\r\n\t},\r\n}, {\r\n\troot = root .. \"/plugins\",\r\n\tdefaults = {\r\n\t\tlazy = true,\r\n\t\tversion = \"*\",\r\n\t},\r\n\tinstall = {\r\n\t\tcolorscheme = { \"catppuccin\" },\r\n\t},\r\n})\r\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe statusline is rendered on startup.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThe statusline is not rendered, instead nvim's default status is shown.\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/31820255/ed50fe43-5b1c-4d5a-897e-c66bfa4da7a9)\r\n",
