            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nThere are several things to unpack here:\r\n- First, I'd **strongly** suggest to not lazy load any UI related plugin (that is, which is expected to be active right after Neovim has started).\r\n- Second, reproducible example contains code which is not executable in fresh setup: `local config = require(\"config\")`.\r\n- Third, reproducible steps do not use latest 'mini.nvim' version (that is, `main` branch), but latest stable release (as indicated by `version = \"*\"`). Coincidentally, this issue was solved [two days ago](47b0e0eb9ad70e5bab10f48281e574a68d71f511) just after 0.12.0 stable release.\r\n\r\nSo I'd suggest to either not lazy load 'mini.statusline' (use `lazy = false` similar to how it is done in 'catppuccin/nvim') or use latest `main` (add `version = false` to 'mini.statusline' config).\r\n\r\nClosing as already solved.",
